ropping the score from +0.0 to -2.2, after B5 had already given up 2.9. The engine wanted J5 instead. This was the last real swing: the score stayed between -2.0 and -2.6 through the passes."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "after.py applies one named move to a pasted board, removes captures and prints each group's liberties; libs.py prints group liberties; count.py scores territory with named dead stones. Each works on the current position for a move the player supplied (the shell loops only call after.py once per hand-picked candidate), with no ranking of moves and no lookahead.", "stop": false}}